
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G H : Points
A,C,B are collinear [00]
CA = CB [01]
EA ∥ BD [02]
ED ∥ BA [03]
E,D,F are collinear [04]
FD = FE [05]
G,C,E are collinear [06]
G,A,D are collinear [07]
H,B,F are collinear [08]
A,H,D are collinear [09]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. A,C,B are collinear [00] & CA = CB [01] ⇒  C is midpoint of AB [10]
002. E,D,F are collinear [04] & FD = FE [05] ⇒  F is midpoint of ED [11]
003. C is midpoint of AB [10] & F is midpoint of ED [11] ⇒  AB:DE = CA:FD [12]
004. BD ∥ AE [02] & DE ∥ AB [03] ⇒  ∠BDE = ∠EAB [13]
005. DE ∥ AB [03] ⇒  ∠BED = ∠EBA [14]
006. ∠BDE = ∠EAB [13] & ∠BED = ∠EBA [14] (Similar Triangles)⇒  ED = BA [15]
007. ∠BDE = ∠EAB [13] & ∠BED = ∠EBA [14] (Similar Triangles)⇒  BD = EA [16]
008. AB:DE = CA:FD [12] & ED = BA [15] ⇒  CA = FD [17]
009. A,C,B are collinear [00] & E,D,F are collinear [04] & AB ∥ DE [03] & AE ∥ BD [02] ⇒  ∠CAE = ∠FDB [18]
010. CA = FD [17] & BD = EA [16] & ∠CAE = ∠FDB [18] (SAS)⇒  ∠ACE = ∠DFB [19]
011. G,C,E are collinear [06] & H,B,F are collinear [08] & ∠ACE = ∠DFB [19] & A,C,B are collinear [00] & E,D,F are collinear [04] & DE ∥ AB [03] ⇒  GE ∥ HF [20]
012. A,H,D are collinear [09] & G,A,D are collinear [07] ⇒  D,G,H are collinear [21]
013. GE ∥ HF [20] & D,G,H are collinear [21] & E,D,F are collinear [04] ⇒  FD:FE = HD:HG [22]
014. FD:FE = HD:HG [22] & FD = FE [05] ⇒  HD = HG
==========================
